late in the campaign of Gears of War  Marcus Fenix kicks in the front door of  his childhood home the wallpaper is  peeling the furniture is in disarray and  a fine layer of dust blankets every  surface from the ceiling to the floor  returning to a dilapidated family home  serves as a poetic echo of the task at  hand many members of developer the  coalition worked on the original gears  of war and this remaster is the studio's  first release before it launches Gears  of War 4 and although the studio has  created a faithful homage to the game  that started it all they neglected to  clean up a few things in the process  there's a lot of history here a lot of  lies - well you've got some nerve  soldier Gears of War Ultimate Edition  lets you cheat time and travel back to  2006 when you first saw Phoenix skulking  in shadowy jelsa because of the new  resolution Gears of War Ultimate Edition  fills in cracks and polishes paintwork  to preserve our ever so fragile  nostalgia I played Gears of War on Xbox  360 recently and the differences here  are apparent Ultimate Edition removes  the muddy textures shiny faces and bleak  environments of the original replacing  them with detailed landscapes and  brighter hues the coalition remade every  cutscene and even though I've seen them  before the new skin makes it feel like  the first time again  an Ultimate Edition doesn't just change  things on a visual level the original  Gears of War marked the pinnacle of  third-person shooting at its time and in  2015 that cover based combat is still at  the top of its class the campaign still  feels smooth and fluid and I noticed it  right away  Ultimate Edition is also a reminder of  how much I'd forgotten about the first  years the campaign is much more horror  driven than its sequels with haunting  corridors and dim basements giving way  to shrieking monsters emerging from the  ground this is a story about a ragtag  group of heroes long before we saw them  amidst the chaos of an all-out war the  characters don't have too much depth for  them here and mainly serve as vehicles  for the action but the campaign serves  as a reminder of when we first saw them  to have Marcus he'll get over it and  then I jumped a multiplayer and it's 60  FPS all of my muscle memory came back I  hip fired the nation' perfected active  reload times and dodged between cover as  if it were 9 years ago there are two new  game modes here including the  traditional team deathmatch and king of  the hill and they're both welcome  additions to this fluid new incarnation  Gears of War Ultimate Edition doesn't  just look like my nostalgia remembers it  also feels like it too but despite how  great Altima Titian looks and feels it  hasn't completely erased the original  versions blemishes the gears franchise  is always catered to a cooperative  experience and the remaster is no  exception  throughout my time with the campaign my  AI partner Dom Santiago often made  things difficult for me he deliberately  wandered into the shadows when the  objective was to stay in the light he  walked into the path of my gun obscuring  my view numerous times and often when my  progress relied on the AI nothing  happened and I had to reload my check  one  the latter was a frequent problem  throughout my campaign the first Gears  isn't always obvious about where to go  next and the remaster has kept that  aspect intact  i reloaded checkpoints a total of five  times before I reached act 5  all because cutscenes wouldn't trigger  or a wall wouldn't crumble on cue it's  one thing to lose progress because of  death it's another to lose it because of  design errors but despite these flaws  Gears of War Ultimate Edition is still a  faithful remaster of a nine year old  game  the return trip might reveal a few more  cracks than we remember but it also  serves as a shield for our nostalgia and  as remakes go that's worth noting  the or  do this  you
 

